@startuml
title Type/Definition document registration - issue 76
autonumber
actor "Platform Engineer/Admin" as PE
boundary Console
boundary HTTP
control Catalog
database Repository
PE -> Console: Upload or paste YAML/JSON
Console -> Console: UTF-8/size/single document/unique keys
opt Resource Definition file
PE -> Console: Check configuration
Console -> HTTP: POST resource-definitions/import/prepare
HTTP -> Catalog: PrepareDefinitionDocument (scoped)
Catalog -> Catalog: Inspect Git url/ref/path -> exact pin
Catalog -> Catalog: Validate full canonical Definition
Catalog --> HTTP: canonical draft + source/commit summary
HTTP --> Console: prepared result (no Definition write)
Console -> Console: Invalidate on edits/scope; discard stale replies
end
PE -> Console: Register checked configuration
Console -> HTTP: POST .../import (strict JSON body)
HTTP -> Catalog: ImportResourceType / ImportResourceDefinition
Catalog -> Catalog: Existing registration validation
Catalog -> Repository: Insert-only registration
alt New key
Repository --> Catalog: committed
Catalog --> HTTP: CREATED
else Duplicate (including insert race)
Catalog -> Repository: Read winner in Organization
Repository --> Catalog: current configuration
Catalog -> Catalog: Compare normalized public contract/defaults
Catalog --> HTTP: REUSED or CONFLICT + field paths (no writes)
end
HTTP --> Console: result
Console --> PE: Keep content and show result
PE -> Console: Download displayed Type/Definition/revision
opt Definition/revision download
Console -> HTTP: GET resource-definitions/{key}/document?revision=id
HTTP -> Catalog: Export scoped saved Definition/revision
Catalog -> Repository: Read saved source metadata (no Git fetch)
Catalog --> HTTP: public draft with url/exactCommit/path for Git
HTTP --> Console: portable DefinitionDraft
end
Console -> Console: Allowlist public fields, serialize YAML
Console --> PE: key[-revision].yaml
@enduml
